an executed parity-only tensorized claim is refused: true
a census judgment in the same item answers it: true
obtaining the census and discarding it is still parity-only: true
a census read only to print it is not a judgment: true
every census predicate, constructor and field form is a judgment: true
a constructor of another module is not the census's: true
a top-level helper that judges counts for the item that references it: true
a top-level helper that executes makes its caller an executing item: true
a judgment in ANOTHER item does not reach this one: true
every executor form makes an item executing: true
a module alias of Ll_test is followed: true
an open of Ll_test brings its executors and judgments into scope: true
a source's own binding shadowing an opened judgment is not the judgment: true
a module the source defines under a library's name is the source's, not the library's: true
an item that executes nothing is not read: true
a tensorized claim that asserts no parity is not read: true
a parity claim whose label names no tensorization is not read: true
the mma word reads in Tile_mma, sk_mma, wmma and a tag: true
the mma word does not read inside another word: true
a label's fragments are followed through let-bound names: true
a name the label binds itself shadows the outer binding of that name: true
a pf format is the label, and pf_all2 and gated forms are claims: true
skipped, fail and a source's own p are not claims this reader reads: true
boundary: a tensorization word arriving through a parameter is not read: true
a row naming the claim's label absorbs it: true
a row naming another label absorbs nothing, and is stale: true
a row over a judged file is stale: true
shipping scanner refuses the parity-only tensorized claim: true
shipping scanner accepts the claim under a named exemption: true
shipping scanner accepts the claim once its item judges the census: true
shipping scanner refuses the exemption the judgment left stale: true
shipping scanner refuses a tree where it read no executed tensorized parity claim: true
